===============================
CLI MUSIC PLAYER — FULL SPEC SHEET
(“Next-Gen Terminal Audio System”)
===============================

1. OVERVIEW
--------------------------------
Name: TBA (working title: "AURORA CLI Audio System")
Type: Terminal-based modular music player
Architecture: Client/Server (MPD-inspired core + modern TUI clients)
Primary Goal: High-performance, fully keyboard-driven, scriptable music system with modern audio + streaming support

Core Philosophy:
- Unix-like modularity
- Zero-bloat design
- Everything scriptable
- Instant response UI (<50ms interaction feel)
- Works locally, remotely (SSH), or headless

------------------------------------------------

2. CORE ARCHITECTURE
--------------------------------
AUDIO ENGINE LAYER:
- Decoding via FFmpeg backend
- Optional SoX processing pipeline
- PipeWire / PulseAudio / ALSA output abstraction layer
- JACK support for pro audio mode

DAEMON (aurora-daemon):
- Runs in background
- Handles playback, queue, library, metadata cache
- Exposes UNIX socket + optional TCP API
- Persistent state storage (SQLite + flat cache files)

CLIENTS:
- TUI client (aurora-tui)
- CLI controller (aurora-cli)
- Optional lightweight web/remote client (aurora-remote)

------------------------------------------------

3. CORE PLAYBACK FEATURES
--------------------------------
- Play / Pause / Stop
- Next / Previous track
- Seek (forward/backward precise or jump-based)
- Volume control (software + system mixer integration)
- Playback speed control (0.5x – 2.0x)
- Gapless playback
- Crossfade (configurable 0–12 seconds)
- Repeat modes:
  - Off
  - Track
  - Album
  - Playlist
- Shuffle modes:
  - Random
  - Weighted smart shuffle (based on play history)

------------------------------------------------

